From: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 22:30:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] AP MLD: Refuse a link addition while the link is not started

A link of an AP MLD joins the AP MLD in hostapd_driver_init(), before
hostapd_setup_bss() starts it. While the link waits for an HT scan, ACS
or a DFS CAC, it has no wpa_auth. A Link Reconfiguration Request that
adds such a link passes the checks of
hostapd_parse_link_reconf_req_sta_profile(), and hostapd adds a link
station for it. Where the driver takes that link station, the RSN state
machine holds no authenticator for the link, and the Link
Reconfiguration Response accepts the link without the MLO GTK, IGTK
and BIGTK KDEs that IEEE Std 802.11be-2024, 35.3.6.4 requires for each
added link. Where the driver refuses it, the release of the link
station reports AP-STA-DISCONNECTED for a station that stays
associated.

Refuse the addition of such a link, as for a link that the AP MLD does
not have.

Signed-off-by: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
---
--- a/src/ap/ieee802_11_eht.c
+++ b/src/ap/ieee802_11_eht.c
@@ -2308,6 +2308,12 @@ hostapd_parse_link_reconf_req_sta_profil
 		goto add_to_list;
 	}
 
+	if (reconf_type == EHT_RECONF_TYPE_ADD_LINK && !lhapd->started) {
+		wpa_printf(MSG_DEBUG, "MLD: Link ID=%u not started", link_id);
+		ret = 1; /* reject this per-STA profile */
+		goto add_to_list;
+	}
+
 	lsta = ap_get_sta(lhapd, req->sta_mld_addr);
 
 	if (reconf_type == EHT_RECONF_TYPE_DELETE_LINK) {
